From 09574ab31c8c08a3a079f0f59e89d30d6e48351c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:47:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/tls_mbedtls: report a closed transport as EOF

mbedtls_ssl_read() returns 0 when the read end of the transport was
closed without a CloseNotify, which is a plain end of stream and is
documented as distinct from MBEDTLS_ERR_SSL_PEER_CLOSE_NOTIFY. It is
not > 0, so it reaches handle_tls_error(), which has no case for it and
falls through to the default, logging "mbedtls_ssl_read returned -0x0"
and returning AVERROR(EIO).

http_read_stream() then sees an I/O error rather than an end of stream,
so neither reconnect nor reconnect_at_eof applies and an endless stream
whose server drops the connection ends instead of reconnecting. Return
AVERROR_EOF for that case, as the CloseNotify case already does.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 libavformat/tls_mbedtls.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/libavformat/tls_mbedtls.c
+++ b/libavformat/tls_mbedtls.c
@@ -801,6 +801,9 @@ static int tls_read(URLContext *h, uint8
         return ret;
     }
 
+    if (!ret)
+        return AVERROR_EOF;
+
     return handle_tls_error(h, "mbedtls_ssl_read", ret);
 }
 
